From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: force runtime suspend across system sleep

The controller only has runtime PM ops, and a peripheral kept
runtime-active (the WCD9390 on the AYN Odin 3, held for jack detection)
keeps it active through s2idle, together with the LPASS macro clocks it
uses. Force the runtime suspend across system sleep, so jack detection
keeps working while awake but the ADSP can release LPASS in s2idle.
---
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index d34aff92e..5fd0a56d8 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -1836,6 +1836,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused swrm_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 }
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops swrm_dev_pm_ops = {
+	SET_SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	SET_RUNTIME_PM_OPS(swrm_runtime_suspend, swrm_runtime_resume, NULL)
 };
 
